-- title:
--   For a covering morphism, the augmentation of the Čech complex of free abelian sheaves is an epimorphism
-- statement:
--   Let $\mathcal{C}$ be a category with finite wide pullbacks and a Grothendieck topology $J$ for which sheafification of abelian presheaves exists. Let $f : V \to U$ be a morphism such that the sieve on $U$ generated by $f$ is a $J$-covering sieve. Write $\mathbb{Z}[X]^{\#}$ for the free abelian sheaf on an object $X$, the sheafification of the free abelian presheaf on the presheaf represented by $X$. Then the augmentation of the Čech complex of free abelian sheaves,
--   $$\mathbb{Z}[f]^{\#} : \mathbb{Z}[V]^{\#} \longrightarrow \mathbb{Z}[U]^{\#},$$
--   is an epimorphism in the category of abelian sheaves on $(\mathcal{C}, J)$.
--
--   This is the degree-zero exactness of the augmented Čech resolution $\cdots \to \mathbb{Z}[V \times_U V]^{\#} \to \mathbb{Z}[V]^{\#} \to \mathbb{Z}[U]^{\#} \to 0$, used to compute sheaf cohomology through Čech complexes.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The category is `C : Type (u + 1)` with `[Category.{u} C]` and abelian groups in `AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}`, with `[HasWeakSheafify J AddCommGrpCat.{u + 1}]`. The covering hypothesis is `Sieve.generate (Presieve.singleton f) ∈ J U`. The morphism `cechFreeAug J f : cechFree J f 0 ⟶ (freeAbelianSheafFunctor J).obj U` is the sheafification of the free abelian presheaf map induced by $f$. The Lean name is `CategoryTheory.epi_cechFreeAug`.
-- source:
--   B. Bhatt, P. Scholze, The pro-étale topology for schemes, https://arxiv.org/abs/1309.1198 (v2, 17 Dec 2014). Lean source: idealson-nexources/proetale (fork of chrisflav/proetale by C. Merten, J. Jiang and contributors, Apache-2.0), commit 2983805, file Proetale/Mathlib/CategoryTheory/Sites/SheafCohomology/CechResolution.lean, lines 583-590 (`CategoryTheory.epi_cechFreeAug`).

